  "query_preview": "..\nUpper trough will continue digging into the western states today.\nFog will continue to impact portions of the region through the \nmorning with some locally dense fog, reducing visibility in spots \nto 2 mile or less.\n\nAs the Pacific upper trough moves through the Great Basin, a\nColorado low is expected to develop ahead of it. This will spread\nprecipitation northward, and will generally favor the Yellowstone\nbasin tonight into Monday. Splitting in the upper trough near the\nCanadian boarder will keep cold air from being drawn southward, \nand result in little to no mixed precipitation or snow. As the \nsurface low deepens, an increase in winds will result by Monday \nafternoon.\n\nA progressive, unsettled pattern will keep next week interesting\nwith repeated upper level troughs.\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS:\n\nNo changes to NBM.\nA lot of uncertainty regarding fog, low cloud and precipitation \ntoday.",
